                        "sense_id": "1e7870a2-092a-33e3-8578-fb1bfb51ca6d",
                        "entry_id": "6c487284-a273-37d3-bfbe-34332833d46c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A member of a secretive Ismaili Shiite community based mainly in the Middle East, specifically Lebanon, Syria, and Israel."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1a66bbf0-85c1-4053-9564-a3756e25b082",
                                "sense_id": "1e7870a2-092a-33e3-8578-fb1bfb51ca6d",
                                "text": "At Acre, 15,000 Druzes elected a six-member council comprising sheiks and mukhtars, their first official representative body since the establishment of Israel."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "895d36d3-d09b-47dc-8ff0-f83246da8b60",
                                "sense_id": "1e7870a2-092a-33e3-8578-fb1bfb51ca6d",
                                "text": "This backlash also fails to take into account that Israel, for all its faults, is a multicultural society where almost half of graduating doctors today are Arabs or Druze."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
